      "content": "I've heard some people say those McKinsey or BCG reports are a bit selective in what they measure, or that they confuse correlation with causation—like, maybe successful companies just happen to be the ones that prioritize DEI, rather than the DEI actually causing the success. On the flip side, some boards are looking at the potential downsides, like social friction or a focus on identity over meritocracy, which can hurt productivity. Why aren't those counter-arguments appearing in the \"consensus\" you mentioned earlier?",
